# After opening a pull request

Every time you open a PR (`gh pr create` or equivalent), immediately run the
setup script against the PR you just created, from the repo root:

```bash
.cursor/scripts/pr-setup.sh <pr-url>
```

The script assigns the pull request's author, adds the PR to the `Gamaliel Roadmap`
project (org `gamaliel-ai`, project number 1), sets Status to **In progress**,
sets Sprint to whichever iteration covers today, and sets **Project Start date**
to today. The author comes from `gh pr view <url> --json author`. The script
does not assign `@me` and does not hardcode a login.

When `GH_PROJECT_TOKEN` is set, the script passes it only to assignment and
Roadmap project commands (`GH_TOKEN="$GH_PROJECT_TOKEN" gh ...`). That value
is a fine-grained token owned by the `belovedbot` machine user, with Projects,
Pull requests, and Issues read/write on gamaliel-ai. It is not exported for
the rest of the script. If assignment or a Roadmap command fails, the script
prints an error and exits non-zero. It does not fall back to another token.
Report that error. Do not retry with a personal token or `gh auth refresh`.

Run it as a separate command after `gh pr create` returns, so a failure in the
setup step never hides the PR URL. Report the PR URL and the sprint it landed in.
